// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/ MPL-2.0
//@version=6
// MSS Sweeps (MPC) — the sweep-and-reclaim TRIGGER, driven by OUR market structure.
//
// WHAT THIS IS. The idea comes from "MSS Sweeps [LuxAlgo]" (kept alongside as
// mss_sweeps_luxalgo.pine, third-party, read-only): after a continuation break, remember the
// protected swing that break left behind, and signal when price WICKS through that swing and
// CLOSES back on the right side of it. This file keeps that trigger and throws away their
// structure entirely.
//
// WHAT CHANGED, and it is all of the structure. Their internal structure is a one-sided leg
// detector at length 5 with its own CHOCH/BOS state machine. Ours is the canonical
// pivot-seeded, pullback-confirmed engine. Consequences worth knowing before reading a chart:
//   - the protected level is our iHL / iLH, confirmed by the pullback rule, not their leg flip
//   - their BOS reads the LIVE close, so it can appear and vanish intrabar; every one of our
//     iBOS/iSOS fires under barstate.isconfirmed, so nothing here repaints
//   - we have a SECOND DEGREE of structure (external, majorLength 15) and they have none.
//     That is what the trend filter below is built on
//
// ⚠ THE ENGINE BLOCK IS indicators/engines/structure_engine.pine LINES 27-1044, with EXACTLY
// ONE LINE CHANGED. Regenerate in two steps:
//     sed -n '27,1044p' structure_engine.pine
//     then change `bool internalActive = showInternal` to `bool internalActive = true`
// Any structure change lands there FIRST and flows here line-for-line. Never fix a structure
// bug in this file — engines/market_structure/ is canonical and this file must not become a
// second implementation of it.
//
// ⚠ WHY THAT ONE LINE. In structure_engine.pine the internal state machine is gated on the
// "Show Internal Structure" DISPLAY toggle, so unticking it to clean up the chart stops every
// signal here. Forced true: the toggle now controls drawing only. The engine gates its own
// internal labels and lines on `showInternal` separately, so all three Market Structure
// display boxes can be unticked for a clean chart and the sweeps keep firing. This is the
// only line that differs and it must be re-applied after any regeneration.
//
// ✅ COMPILES on TradingView (Aaron, 2026-08-13). ⚠ NOTHING HERE IS MEASURED — compiling says
// the syntax is valid and nothing else. No Strategy Tester run, no parity gate, no Python
// port. Every default below is a starting point chosen to be legible, not an optimum. The
// stats table exists so the trend filter can be judged from a real chart rather than argued
// about — read "raw" against "signalled" before believing the filter helps.
indicator("MSS Sweeps (MPC)", "MSS Sweeps (MPC)", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500)

//============================================================
//  SMC SETTINGS (hardcoded)
//============================================================
int   majorLength = 15
color bullColor   = color.blue
color bearColor   = color.red
color iBullColor  = bullColor
color iBearColor  = bearColor

//============================================================
//  MARKET STRUCTURE — input selection (mirrors mpc_assistant.pine's GRP_STRUCT)
//============================================================
var GRP_STRUCT = "Market Structure"
string structLabelSize  = input.string("Small", "Structure Label Size",    group = GRP_STRUCT, options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], display = display.none)
bool   showExternal     = input.bool(true,      "Show External Structure", group = GRP_STRUCT, display = display.none)
bool   showInternal     = input.bool(true,      "Show Internal Structure", group = GRP_STRUCT, display = display.none)
bool   showHistoricalInternal = input.bool(false, "Show Historic Internal Structure", group = GRP_STRUCT, tooltip = "Keep internal structure labels and lines from previous swing ranges on the chart. Off = only show current swing range internals.", display = display.none)
bool   showSwingLabels  = input.bool(true, "Show Swing Point Labels", group = GRP_STRUCT, tooltip = "Off = hide ASH/ASL, HH/HL, LH/LL and the internal swing point labels, leaving only BOS/SOS and iBOS/iSOS on the chart. The structure engine keeps running exactly as before — fibs, order blocks and the confirmation table are unaffected.", display = display.none)
float  pbBuffer         = 0.0

f_structSize() =>
    not showExternal ? size.auto : structLabelSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : structLabelSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : structLabelSize == "Large" ? size.large : structLabelSize == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.small

// Swing-point labels are hidden by making their text transparent, not by skipping
// their creation. The label objects still exist and the engine's state is untouched,
// so structure tracking, fibs, OBs and the table behave identically either way.
f_swingCol(color c) =>
    showSwingLabels ? c : color(na)

//============================================================
//  SMC STRUCTURE TYPE
//============================================================
type SMCStructure
    int    length
    float  ash             = na
    int    ash_loc         = na
    string ash_type        = ""
    line   ash_line        = na
    label  ash_lbl         = na
    float  asl             = na
    int    asl_loc         = na
    string asl_type        = ""
    line   asl_line        = na
    label  asl_lbl         = na
    float  last_conf_high     = na
    int    last_conf_high_loc = na
    float  last_conf_low      = na
    int    last_conf_low_loc  = na
    int    dir            = 0
    bool   choch_lock     = false
    line   choch_ref      = na
    int    pb_mode        = 0
    int    pb_count       = 0
    float  pb_level       = na
    float  pb_extreme     = na
    int    pb_extreme_loc = na
    line   pb_line        = na
    bool   pb_started     = false
    float  pb_last_qualify_close = na
    float  pb_last_qualify_high  = na
    float  pb_extreme_close      = na
    float  prev_close     = na
    float  prev_high      = na
    float  prev_low       = na
    bool   seeded         = false
    bool   bull_bos       = false
    float  bull_bos_high  = na
    int    bull_bos_h_loc = na
    float  bull_bos_low   = na
    int    bull_bos_l_loc = na
    bool   bear_bos       = false
    float  bear_bos_high  = na
    int    bear_bos_h_loc = na
    float  bear_bos_low   = na
    int    bear_bos_l_loc = na
    bool   new_swing_high = false
    bool   new_swing_low  = false
    bool   bull_sos       = false
    bool   bear_sos       = false

// prefix: "" for external, "i" for internal
// bull_col / bear_col allow per-instance colors
method create_ash(SMCStructure st, float val, int loc, color col, bool solid, string prefix) =>
    if not na(st.ash_line)
        line.delete(st.ash_line)
    if not na(st.ash_lbl)
        label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
        st.ash_lbl := na
    st.ash      := val
    st.ash_loc  := loc
    st.ash_type := ""
    st.ash_lbl  := label.new(loc, val, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
    st.ash_line := line.new(loc, val, bar_index, val, color=col, style=solid ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed, width=solid ? 2 : 1)

method create_asl(SMCStructure st, float val, int loc, color col, bool solid, string prefix) =>
    if not na(st.asl_line)
        line.delete(st.asl_line)
    if not na(st.asl_lbl)
        label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
        st.asl_lbl := na
    st.asl      := val
    st.asl_loc  := loc
    st.asl_type := ""
    st.asl_lbl  := label.new(loc, val, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
    st.asl_line := line.new(loc, val, bar_index, val, color=col, style=solid ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed, width=solid ? 2 : 1)

// process() now accepts prefix + bull/bear colors so both instances share one method
method process(SMCStructure st, float ph_val, float pl_val, string prefix, color bull_col, color bear_col) =>

    st.bull_bos := false
    st.bear_bos := false
    st.new_swing_high := false
    st.new_swing_low  := false
    st.bull_sos := false
    st.bear_sos := false

    bool is_inside = false
    if not na(st.prev_high) and not na(st.prev_low)
        is_inside := high < st.prev_high and low > st.prev_low

    if st.choch_lock
        if st.dir == 1 and not na(pl_val)
            st.choch_lock := false
        else if st.dir == -1 and not na(ph_val)
            st.choch_lock := false

    if st.pb_mode == 1
        if not st.pb_started
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
        else
            bool extreme_updated_1 = false
            if na(st.pb_extreme) or high > st.pb_extreme
                st.pb_extreme            := high
                st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
                st.pb_extreme_close      := na
                st.pb_count              := 0
                st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
                st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
                extreme_updated_1        := true
            bool extreme_is_bearish_1 = extreme_updated_1 and close < open
            bool is_candle1_1 = na(st.pb_last_qualify_close) and not extreme_updated_1
            if (not is_inside or is_candle1_1) and (not extreme_updated_1 or extreme_is_bearish_1)
                float threshold = na(st.pb_last_qualify_high) ? st.pb_extreme : st.pb_last_qualify_high
                if close < threshold - pbBuffer
                    st.pb_count              += 1
                    st.pb_last_qualify_close := close
                    st.pb_last_qualify_high  := low
            if st.pb_count >= 3 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
                if not na(st.ash_line)
                    line.delete(st.ash_line)
                if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                    label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
                st.ash      := st.pb_extreme
                st.ash_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
                st.ash_type := "LOCKED"
                st.ash_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bear_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
                st.ash_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                st.new_swing_high := true
                st.pb_mode    := 0
                st.pb_count   := 0
                st.choch_lock := false

    else if st.pb_mode == -1
        if not st.pb_started
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
        else
            bool extreme_updated_m1 = false
            if na(st.pb_extreme) or low < st.pb_extreme
                st.pb_extreme            := low
                st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
                st.pb_extreme_close      := na
                st.pb_count              := 0
                st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
                st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
                extreme_updated_m1       := true
            bool extreme_is_bullish_m1 = extreme_updated_m1 and close > open
            bool is_candle1_m1 = na(st.pb_last_qualify_close) and not extreme_updated_m1
            if (not is_inside or is_candle1_m1) and (not extreme_updated_m1 or extreme_is_bullish_m1)
                float threshold = na(st.pb_last_qualify_high) ? st.pb_extreme : st.pb_last_qualify_high
                if close > threshold + pbBuffer
                    st.pb_count              += 1
                    st.pb_last_qualify_close := close
                    st.pb_last_qualify_high  := high
            if st.pb_count >= 3 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
                if not na(st.asl_line)
                    line.delete(st.asl_line)
                if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                    label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
                st.asl      := st.pb_extreme
                st.asl_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
                st.asl_type := "LOCKED"
                st.asl_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bull_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
                st.asl_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bull_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
                st.new_swing_low := true
                st.pb_mode    := 0
                st.pb_count   := 0
                st.choch_lock := false

    st.prev_close := close
    st.prev_high  := high
    st.prev_low   := low

    if na(st.ash) and na(st.asl) and not st.seeded
        if not na(ph_val)
            st.create_ash(ph_val, bar_index[st.length], bear_col, false, prefix)
            st.dir := -1
        else if not na(pl_val)
            st.create_asl(pl_val, bar_index[st.length], bull_col, false, prefix)
            st.dir := 1

    if not st.seeded
        if not na(st.ash) and na(st.asl)
            float seed_low = low
            int   seed_loc = bar_index
            int   lb       = math.min(bar_index, 500)
            for i = 0 to lb
                if low[i] < seed_low
                    seed_low := low[i]
                    seed_loc := bar_index - i
            if seed_low < st.ash
                st.asl      := seed_low
                st.asl_loc  := seed_loc
                st.asl_type := ""
                st.asl_line := line.new(seed_loc, seed_low, bar_index, seed_low, color=bull_col, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
                st.asl_lbl  := label.new(seed_loc, seed_low, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bull_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
                st.seeded := true
        else if not na(st.asl) and na(st.ash)
            float seed_high = high
            int   seed_loc  = bar_index
            int   lb        = math.min(bar_index, 500)
            for i = 0 to lb
                if high[i] > seed_high
                    seed_high := high[i]
                    seed_loc  := bar_index - i
            if seed_high > st.asl
                st.ash      := seed_high
                st.ash_loc  := seed_loc
                st.ash_type := ""
                st.ash_line := line.new(seed_loc, seed_high, bar_index, seed_high, color=bear_col, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
                st.ash_lbl  := label.new(seed_loc, seed_high, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                st.seeded := true
        else if not na(st.ash) and not na(st.asl)
            st.seeded := true

    if na(st.last_conf_high) and na(st.last_conf_low)
        if not na(ph_val) and not na(st.ash) and st.ash_type == "" and st.pb_mode == 0
            if ph_val > st.ash
                st.create_ash(ph_val, bar_index[st.length], bear_col, false, prefix)
        if not na(pl_val) and not na(st.asl) and st.asl_type == "" and st.pb_mode == 0
            if pl_val < st.asl
                st.create_asl(pl_val, bar_index[st.length], bull_col, false, prefix)

    bool ash_broken = not na(st.ash) and close > st.ash
    bool asl_broken = not na(st.asl) and close < st.asl

    if ash_broken
        st.bull_bos := true
        st.bull_bos_high  := st.ash
        st.bull_bos_h_loc := st.ash_loc

        bool was_in_bear_pb = st.pb_mode == -1 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
        st.pb_mode  := 0
        st.pb_count := 0

        bool   is_choch    = st.dir == -1
        string brk_lbl_txt = is_choch ? prefix + "SOS" : prefix + "BOS"
        if is_choch
            st.bull_sos := true
        int    mid_x       = math.round((st.ash_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label.new(mid_x, st.ash, "\n" + brk_lbl_txt, color=color(na), textcolor=bull_col, style=label.style_label_down, size=size.tiny)

        if is_choch
            st.choch_lock := true

        bool brk_already_conf_high = (st.ash == st.last_conf_high and st.ash_loc == st.last_conf_high_loc)
        if not na(st.ash_lbl)
            label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
        if not brk_already_conf_high
            bool   brk_is_hh  = na(st.last_conf_high) or st.ash >= st.last_conf_high
            string brk_high_t = brk_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH"
            color  brk_high_c = brk_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col
            label.new(st.ash_loc, st.ash, brk_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(brk_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())

        if not na(st.ash_line)
            line.set_style(st.ash_line, line.style_solid)
            line.set_color(st.ash_line, bull_col)
            line.set_width(st.ash_line, 2)
            line.set_x2(st.ash_line, bar_index)
            st.ash_line := na

        st.last_conf_high     := st.ash
        st.last_conf_high_loc := st.ash_loc
        st.ash_lbl            := na
        st.ash                := na
        st.dir                := 1

        if was_in_bear_pb
            st.bull_bos_low   := st.pb_extreme
            st.bull_bos_l_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            if not na(st.asl_line)
                line.delete(st.asl_line)
            if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
            bool   pb_is_hl = is_choch ? false : (na(st.last_conf_low) or st.pb_extreme >= st.last_conf_low)
            // On an SOS (fast reversal) the extreme is only the ACTIVE swing low —
            // it prints as ASL and is confirmed to HL/LL by the NEXT bullish break.
            string pb_low_t = is_choch ? prefix + "ASL" : (pb_is_hl ? prefix + "HL" : prefix + "LL")
            color  pb_low_c = is_choch ? bull_col : (pb_is_hl ? bull_col : bear_col)
            st.asl      := st.pb_extreme
            st.asl_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.asl_type := "LOCKED"
            st.asl_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bull_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            st.asl_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, "\n" + pb_low_t, color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(pb_low_c), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
            if not is_choch
                st.last_conf_low     := st.pb_extreme
                st.last_conf_low_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_mode               := 1
            st.pb_started            := true
        else
            if not na(st.asl)
                bool already_conf_low = (st.asl == st.last_conf_low and st.asl_loc == st.last_conf_low_loc)
                if not already_conf_low
                    bool   old_is_hl = is_choch ? false : (na(st.last_conf_low) or st.asl >= st.last_conf_low)
                    string old_low_t = old_is_hl ? prefix + "HL" : prefix + "LL"
                    color  old_low_c = old_is_hl ? bull_col : bear_col
                    if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
                    label.new(st.asl_loc, st.asl, "\n" + old_low_t, color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(old_low_c), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
                    st.last_conf_low     := st.asl
                    st.last_conf_low_loc := st.asl_loc
                else
                    if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
                if not na(st.asl_line)
                    line.delete(st.asl_line)
                st.asl_line := na
                st.asl_lbl  := na
                st.asl      := na

            float lowest_val = low
            int   lowest_loc = bar_index
            int   bars_back  = na(st.last_conf_high_loc) ? bar_index : bar_index - st.last_conf_high_loc
            if bars_back > 0
                int max_lb = math.min(math.min(bars_back, 1490), bar_index)
                for i = 0 to max_lb
                    if low[i] < lowest_val
                        lowest_val := low[i]
                        lowest_loc := bar_index - i

            st.bull_bos_low   := lowest_val
            st.bull_bos_l_loc := lowest_loc

            st.asl      := lowest_val
            st.asl_loc  := lowest_loc
            st.asl_type := ""
            st.asl_line := line.new(lowest_loc, lowest_val, bar_index, lowest_val, color=bull_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            if lowest_val != st.last_conf_low
                st.asl_lbl := label.new(lowest_loc, lowest_val, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bull_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
            else
                st.asl_lbl := na

            st.pb_mode               := 1
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true

    else if asl_broken
        st.bear_bos := true
        st.bear_bos_low   := st.asl
        st.bear_bos_l_loc := st.asl_loc

        bool was_in_bull_pb = st.pb_mode == 1 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
        st.pb_mode  := 0
        st.pb_count := 0

        bool   is_choch    = st.dir == 1
        string brk_lbl_txt = is_choch ? prefix + "SOS" : prefix + "BOS"
        if is_choch
            st.bear_sos := true
        int    mid_x       = math.round((st.asl_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label.new(mid_x, st.asl, brk_lbl_txt + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=bear_col, style=label.style_label_up, size=size.tiny)

        if is_choch
            st.choch_lock := true

        bool brk_already_conf_low = (st.asl == st.last_conf_low and st.asl_loc == st.last_conf_low_loc)
        if not na(st.asl_lbl)
            label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
        if not brk_already_conf_low
            bool   brk_is_hl = na(st.last_conf_low) or st.asl >= st.last_conf_low
            string brk_low_t = brk_is_hl ? prefix + "HL" : prefix + "LL"
            label.new(st.asl_loc, st.asl, "\n" + brk_low_t, color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())

        if not na(st.asl_line)
            line.set_style(st.asl_line, line.style_solid)
            line.set_color(st.asl_line, bear_col)
            line.set_width(st.asl_line, 2)
            line.set_x2(st.asl_line, bar_index)
            st.asl_line := na

        st.last_conf_low     := st.asl
        st.last_conf_low_loc := st.asl_loc
        st.asl_lbl           := na
        st.asl               := na
        st.dir               := -1

        if was_in_bull_pb
            st.bear_bos_high  := st.pb_extreme
            st.bear_bos_h_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            if not na(st.ash_line)
                line.delete(st.ash_line)
            if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
            bool   pb_is_hh  = na(st.last_conf_high) or st.pb_extreme >= st.last_conf_high
            // On an SOS (fast reversal) the extreme is only the ACTIVE swing high —
            // it prints as ASH and is confirmed to HH/LH by the NEXT bearish break.
            string pb_high_t = is_choch ? prefix + "ASH" : (pb_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH")
            color  pb_high_c = is_choch ? bear_col : (pb_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col)
            st.ash      := st.pb_extreme
            st.ash_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.ash_type := "LOCKED"
            st.ash_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bear_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            st.ash_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, pb_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(pb_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
            if not is_choch
                st.last_conf_high     := st.pb_extreme
                st.last_conf_high_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_mode               := -1
            st.pb_started            := true
        else
            float highest_val = high
            int   highest_loc = bar_index
            int   bars_back   = na(st.last_conf_low_loc) ? bar_index : bar_index - st.last_conf_low_loc
            if bars_back > 0
                int max_lb = math.min(math.min(bars_back, 1490), bar_index)
                for i = 0 to max_lb
                    if high[i] > highest_val
                        highest_val := high[i]
                        highest_loc := bar_index - i

            if not na(st.ash)
                bool already_conf_high = (st.ash == st.last_conf_high and st.ash_loc == st.last_conf_high_loc)
                if not already_conf_high
                    bool   old_is_hh  = is_choch ? true : (na(st.last_conf_high) or st.ash >= st.last_conf_high)
                    string old_high_t = old_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH"
                    color  old_high_c = old_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col
                    if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
                    label.new(st.ash_loc, st.ash, old_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(old_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                    st.last_conf_high     := st.ash
                    st.last_conf_high_loc := st.ash_loc
                else
                    if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
                if not na(st.ash_line)
                    line.delete(st.ash_line)
                st.ash_line := na
                st.ash_lbl  := na
                st.ash      := na
            else
                // Neither an active pullback high nor a confirmed ASH was available to
                // promote — use the actual highest point since the last confirmed low so
                // a genuine swing high still gets confirmed instead of silently vanishing.
                bool   fallback_is_hh  = na(st.last_conf_high) or highest_val >= st.last_conf_high
                string fallback_high_t = fallback_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH"
                color  fallback_high_c = fallback_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col
                if highest_val != st.last_conf_high
                    label.new(highest_loc, highest_val, fallback_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(fallback_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                    st.last_conf_high     := highest_val
                    st.last_conf_high_loc := highest_loc

            st.bear_bos_high  := highest_val
            st.bear_bos_h_loc := highest_loc

            st.ash      := highest_val
            st.ash_loc  := highest_loc
            st.ash_type := ""
            st.ash_line := line.new(highest_loc, highest_val, bar_index, highest_val, color=bear_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            if highest_val != st.last_conf_high
                st.ash_lbl := label.new(highest_loc, highest_val, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
            else
                st.ash_lbl := na

            st.pb_mode               := -1
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true

    if not na(st.ash_line)
        line.set_x2(st.ash_line, bar_index)
        if not showExternal
            line.set_color(st.ash_line, color(na))
    if not na(st.asl_line)
        line.set_x2(st.asl_line, bar_index)
        if not showExternal
            line.set_color(st.asl_line, color(na))
    if not showExternal
        if not na(st.ash_lbl)
            label.set_textcolor(st.ash_lbl, color(na))
        if not na(st.asl_lbl)
            label.set_textcolor(st.asl_lbl, color(na))

//============================================================
//  EXECUTION — EXTERNAL STRUCTURE
//============================================================
// External structure engine — majorLength=15, blue/red, prefix ""
var st = SMCStructure.new(majorLength)
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, majorLength, majorLength)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  majorLength, majorLength)
// showExternal off → pass color(na) so ALL lines and labels hidden inside process
// showExternal off but showExternal on → pass color(na) for labels only — handled via ASH/ASL override below
color extBullCol = showExternal ? (showExternal ? bullColor : color(na)) : color(na)
color extBearCol = showExternal ? (showExternal ? bearColor : color(na)) : color(na)
st.process(ph, pl, "", extBullCol, extBearCol)

// After process runs — restore line colors when labels are hidden but structure is visible
if not na(st.ash_line)
    line.set_x2(st.ash_line, bar_index)
    if showExternal and not showExternal
        line.set_color(st.ash_line, bullColor)
if not na(st.asl_line)
    line.set_x2(st.asl_line, bar_index)
    if showExternal and not showExternal
        line.set_color(st.asl_line, bearColor)
if not na(st.ash_lbl)
    label.set_textcolor(st.ash_lbl, showExternal ? f_swingCol(bearColor) : color(na))
if not na(st.asl_lbl)
    label.set_textcolor(st.asl_lbl, showExternal ? f_swingCol(bullColor) : color(na))

//============================================================
//  EXECUTION — INTERNAL STRUCTURE
//============================================================
// Internal structure — Step 2: pullback tracking to confirm iSH / iSL

// ── State ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
var int   i_mode           = 0
var bool  i_seeded         = false

// Pullback tracking
var float i_pb_extreme     = na
var int   i_pb_extreme_loc = na
var int   i_pb_count       = 0
var bool  i_pb_started     = false
var float i_pb_lqc         = na
var float i_pb_lqh         = na
var float i_prev_high      = na
var float i_prev_low       = na

// Active swing level (iSH or iSL)
var float i_sw_price       = na
var int   i_sw_loc         = na
var line  i_sw_line        = na
var label i_sw_lbl         = na

// Pre-declared locals (Pine v6)
var bool  i_ext_chg        = false
var bool  i_is_inside      = false
var bool  i_ext_dir        = false
var bool  i_is_c1          = false
var float i_thresh         = na

var float i_tracked_ext     = na
var int   i_tracked_ext_loc = na
var int   i_last_mode       = 0   // remembers what mode confirmed the swing
var bool  i_had_bos         = false
var int   i_bos_dir         = 0
var string i_h_lbl          = ""
var color  i_h_col          = color.black
var string i_l_lbl          = ""
var color  i_l_col          = color.black
var int   i_mid             = 0
var int   i_mid2            = 0
var float i_last_hl         = na   // last confirmed iHL price (for iSOS in bullish cycle)

var float i_last_lh         = na   // last confirmed iLH price (for iSOS in bearish cycle)
var int   i_last_hl_loc     = na
var int   i_last_lh_loc     = na

var float i_sos_watch_hh    = na
var int   i_sos_watch_hh_loc= na
var float i_sos_watch_ll    = na
var int   i_sos_watch_ll_loc= na

float i_lbl_y_offset = syminfo.mintick * 20   // vertical offset for iBOS/iSOS (smaller number = closer to the line)

// Internal structure is naturally scoped to the current active external swing —
// it resets on every external SOS/CHoCH (see block right below).
// 🔴 THE ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM structure_engine.pine. There this reads
// `= showInternal`, which makes a DISPLAY toggle switch off the state machine. That is
// tolerable in a file whose only output is drawing; it is not tolerable here, where every
// signal reads this engine — unticking "Show Internal Structure" to clean up the chart would
// silently stop the indicator. Forced true, so the toggle now controls ONLY what is drawn:
// the engine already gates its own labels and lines on `showInternal` separately, so with this
// off the structure disappears and the sweeps keep working. Re-apply after any regeneration.
bool internalActive = true

// Tracks every internal-structure label/line drawn during the current external
// swing, so they can be wiped when a new swing starts (unless showHistoricalInternal is on).
var array<label> intHistLabels = array.new<label>()
var array<line>  intHistLines  = array.new<line>()

// ── Stop internal tracking on external SOS ───────────────

if internalActive and (st.bull_bos or st.bear_bos or st.bull_sos or st.bear_sos)
    if not na(i_sw_line)
        line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
        i_sw_line := na
    i_sw_lbl          := na
    i_sw_price        := na
    i_mode            := 0
    i_seeded          := false
    i_pb_count        := 0
    i_pb_started      := false
    i_tracked_ext     := na
    i_tracked_ext_loc := na
    i_last_hl         := na
    i_last_lh         := na
    i_had_bos         := false
    i_sos_watch_hh    := na
    i_sos_watch_ll    := na
    // Past swing just ended — wipe its internal structure unless history is enabled
    if not showHistoricalInternal
        if array.size(intHistLabels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(intHistLabels) - 1
                label.delete(array.get(intHistLabels, i))
        if array.size(intHistLines) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(intHistLines) - 1
                line.delete(array.get(intHistLines, i))
    array.clear(intHistLabels)
    array.clear(intHistLines)

// ── Track prev bar ────────────────────────────────────────
if internalActive
    i_prev_high := high
    i_prev_low  := low


// ── Seed on new external swing ────────────────────────────
if internalActive
    if st.new_swing_low and not st.bull_sos and not st.bear_sos
        i_mode            := 1
        i_seeded          := true
        i_had_bos         := false
        i_bos_dir         := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_extreme      := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_mode       := 1
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na
        i_sos_watch_ll    := na
    else if st.new_swing_high and not st.bull_sos and not st.bear_sos
        i_mode            := -1
        i_seeded          := true
        i_had_bos         := false
        i_bos_dir         := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_extreme      := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na
        i_sos_watch_ll    := na

// ── Mode 1: track upward move → confirm iSH ──────────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_mode == 1
    if not i_pb_started
        i_pb_started     := true
        i_pb_extreme     := high
        i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
        i_pb_count       := 0
        i_pb_lqc         := na
        i_pb_lqh         := na
    else
        // Update extreme if new high
        i_ext_chg := false
        if high > i_pb_extreme
            i_pb_extreme     := high
            i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
            i_pb_count       := 0
            i_pb_lqc         := na
            i_pb_lqh         := na
            i_ext_chg        := true
        // is_inside and qualifying bar checks (exact external rule)
        i_is_inside := not na(i_prev_high) and not na(i_prev_low) and high < i_prev_high and low > i_prev_low
        i_ext_dir   := i_ext_chg and close < open
        i_is_c1     := na(i_pb_lqc) and not i_ext_chg
        if (not i_is_inside or i_is_c1) and (not i_ext_chg or i_ext_dir)
            i_thresh := na(i_pb_lqh) ? i_pb_extreme : i_pb_lqh
            if close < i_thresh - pbBuffer
                i_pb_count += 1
                i_pb_lqc   := close
                i_pb_lqh   := low
        // 3 bars confirmed → iSH
        if i_pb_count >= 3 and not na(i_pb_extreme)
            if not na(i_sw_line)
                line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line  := na
            i_sw_lbl   := na
            i_sw_price := i_pb_extreme
            i_sw_loc   := i_pb_extreme_loc
            // Label: iSH if first swing, iHH if higher than last, iLH if lower
            i_h_lbl := not i_had_bos ? "iSH" : "iHH"
            i_h_col := not i_had_bos ? iBearColor : iBullColor
            i_sw_line  := line.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, bar_index, i_sw_price, color = showInternal ? color.new(i_h_col, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            i_sw_lbl   := label.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, i_h_lbl + "\n", color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(i_h_col, 15)), style = label.style_label_down, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, i_sw_line)
            array.push(intHistLabels, i_sw_lbl)
            i_mode       := 0
            i_pb_count   := 0
            i_pb_started := false

// ── Mode -1: track downward move → confirm iSL ───────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_mode == -1
    if not i_pb_started
        i_pb_started     := true
        i_pb_extreme     := low
        i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
        i_pb_count       := 0
        i_pb_lqc         := na
        i_pb_lqh         := na
    else
        // Update extreme if new low
        i_ext_chg := false
        if low < i_pb_extreme
            i_pb_extreme     := low
            i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
            i_pb_count       := 0
            i_pb_lqc         := na
            i_pb_lqh         := na
            i_ext_chg        := true
        // is_inside and qualifying bar checks
        i_is_inside := not na(i_prev_high) and not na(i_prev_low) and high < i_prev_high and low > i_prev_low
        i_ext_dir   := i_ext_chg and close > open
        i_is_c1     := na(i_pb_lqc) and not i_ext_chg
        if (not i_is_inside or i_is_c1) and (not i_ext_chg or i_ext_dir)
            i_thresh := na(i_pb_lqh) ? i_pb_extreme : i_pb_lqh
            if close > i_thresh + pbBuffer
                i_pb_count += 1
                i_pb_lqc   := close
                i_pb_lqh   := high
        // 3 bars confirmed → iSL
        if i_pb_count >= 3 and not na(i_pb_extreme)
            if not na(i_sw_line)
                line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line  := na
            i_sw_lbl   := na
            i_sw_price := i_pb_extreme
            i_sw_loc   := i_pb_extreme_loc
            // Label: iSL if first swing, iLL if lower than last, iHL if higher
            i_l_lbl := not i_had_bos ? "iSL" : "iLL"
            i_l_col := not i_had_bos ? iBullColor : iBearColor
            i_sw_line  := line.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, bar_index, i_sw_price, color = showInternal ? color.new(i_l_col, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            i_sw_lbl   := label.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, "\n" + i_l_lbl, color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(i_l_col, 15)), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, i_sw_line)
            array.push(intHistLabels, i_sw_lbl)
            i_mode       := 0
            i_pb_count   := 0
            i_pb_started := false

// ── Track extreme while watching (mode 0) ────────────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_mode == 0
    if i_last_mode == 1
        if na(i_tracked_ext) or low < i_tracked_ext
            i_tracked_ext     := low
            i_tracked_ext_loc := bar_index
    else if i_last_mode == -1
        if na(i_tracked_ext) or high > i_tracked_ext
            i_tracked_ext     := high
            i_tracked_ext_loc := bar_index

// ── iBOS / iSOS detection ────────────────────────────────
bool int_bull_break = false
bool int_bear_break = false
bool int_bull_bos   = false
bool int_bull_sos   = false
bool int_bear_bos   = false
bool int_bear_sos   = false
int  int_break_origin_loc = na

if internalActive and i_mode == 0 and i_seeded and not na(i_sw_price) and barstate.isconfirmed
    if close > i_sw_price and i_last_mode == 1
        i_mid := math.round((i_sw_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iBullBOSLbl = label.new(i_mid, i_sw_price + i_lbl_y_offset, "iBOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBullColor : color(na), style = label.style_none, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iBullBOSLbl)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
        i_sw_lbl := na
        if not na(i_tracked_ext)
            line  iHLLine = line.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, bar_index, i_tracked_ext, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBullColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            label iHLLbl  = label.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, "\niHL", color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(iBullColor, 15)), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, iHLLine)
            array.push(intHistLabels, iHLLbl)
            i_last_hl     := i_tracked_ext
            i_last_hl_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc
        
        int_bull_break := true
        int_bull_bos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc

        i_sw_price       := na
        i_tracked_ext    := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_pb_count       := 0
        i_pb_started     := false
        i_pb_lqc         := na
        i_pb_lqh         := na
        i_had_bos        := true
        i_bos_dir        := 1
        i_last_mode      := 1
        i_mode           := 1
        i_sos_watch_ll   := na

    else if close < i_sw_price and i_last_mode == -1
        i_mid2 := math.round((i_sw_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iBearBOSLbl = label.new(i_mid2, i_sw_price, "iBOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBearColor : color(na), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iBearBOSLbl)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
        i_sw_lbl := na
        if not na(i_tracked_ext)
            line  iLHLine = line.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, bar_index, i_tracked_ext, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBearColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            label iLHLbl  = label.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, "iLH\n", color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(iBearColor, 15)), style = label.style_label_down, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, iLHLine)
            array.push(intHistLabels, iLHLbl)
            i_last_lh     := i_tracked_ext
            i_last_lh_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc
            
        int_bear_break := true
        int_bear_bos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc

        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_had_bos         := true
        i_bos_dir         := -1
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_mode            := -1
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na



// ── iSOS detection (watches last iHL / iLH) ──────────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_had_bos and barstate.isconfirmed
    if i_last_mode == 1 and not na(i_last_hl) and close < i_last_hl and i_mode == 0
        i_mid2 := math.round((i_last_hl_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS1Lbl = label.new(i_mid2, i_last_hl, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBearColor : color(na), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS1Line = line.new(i_last_hl_loc, i_last_hl, bar_index, i_last_hl, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBearColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS1Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS1Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
        
        i_sos_watch_hh     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_hh_loc := i_sw_loc
        i_sos_watch_ll     := na
        
        int_bear_break := true
        int_bear_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_mode            := -1

    else if i_last_mode == -1 and not na(i_last_lh) and close > i_last_lh and i_mode == 0
        i_mid := math.round((i_last_lh_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS2Lbl = label.new(i_mid, i_last_lh + i_lbl_y_offset, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBullColor : color(na), style = label.style_none, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS2Line = line.new(i_last_lh_loc, i_last_lh, bar_index, i_last_lh, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBullColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS2Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS2Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
            
        i_sos_watch_ll     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_ll_loc := i_sw_loc
        i_sos_watch_hh     := na
        
        int_bull_break := true
        int_bull_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := 1
        i_mode            := 1

    else if i_last_mode == -1 and not na(i_sos_watch_hh) and close > i_sos_watch_hh and i_mode == 0
        i_mid := math.round((i_sos_watch_hh_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS3Lbl = label.new(i_mid, i_sos_watch_hh + i_lbl_y_offset, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBullColor : color(na), style = label.style_none, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS3Line = line.new(i_sos_watch_hh_loc, i_sos_watch_hh, bar_index, i_sos_watch_hh, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBullColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS3Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS3Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
            
        i_sos_watch_ll     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_ll_loc := i_sw_loc
        
        int_bull_break := true
        int_bull_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := 1
        i_mode            := 1
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na

    else if i_last_mode == 1 and not na(i_sos_watch_ll) and close < i_sos_watch_ll and i_mode == 0
        i_mid2 := math.round((i_sos_watch_ll_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS4Lbl = label.new(i_mid2, i_sos_watch_ll, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBearColor : color(na), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS4Line = line.new(i_sos_watch_ll_loc, i_sos_watch_ll, bar_index, i_sos_watch_ll, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBearColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS4Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS4Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
            
        i_sos_watch_hh     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_hh_loc := i_sw_loc
        
        int_bear_break := true
        int_bear_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_mode            := -1
        i_sos_watch_ll    := na

// ── Update last_mode when mode changes ───────────────────
if internalActive and i_mode != 0
    i_last_mode := i_mode

// ── Extend active swing line every bar ────────────────────
if internalActive and not na(i_sw_line)
    line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)

//============================================================
//  MSS SWEEPS — the trigger layer
//============================================================
// Everything below this line is new. Everything above it is structure_engine.pine.
//
// The sequence, stated once so the code can be read against it:
//   1. our internal engine prints an iBOS (a CONTINUATION break, not a character change)
//   2. that break leaves a protected swing behind it — the iHL under a bull iBOS, the iLH
//      above a bear iBOS. That level is where the stops are
//   3. price WICKS through it and CLOSES back on the original side, with a real body
//   4. that is the signal
// A close THROUGH the level and staying there is not a sweep, it is a failure, and it disarms.

var string GRP_MSS   = "MSS Sweeps"
var string GRP_TREND = "MSS Trend Filter"
var string GRP_MSSTY = "MSS Style"

// ── Trigger shape ────────────────────────────────────────
bool  msShow          = input.bool(true,  "Show MSS sweeps",                group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "The signal itself. Off leaves the protected levels drawn but prints nothing.")
bool  msShowLevel     = input.bool(true,  "Show protected level",           group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "Extend the iHL/iLH the last iBOS left behind, until it is swept, failed, or invalidated.")
bool  msShowFiltered  = input.bool(true,  "Show filtered-out sweeps (grey)",group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "Draw the sweeps the trend filter REJECTED, in grey. This is how you judge whether the filter is helping or just cutting the sample. Turn it off once you have decided.")
int   msMaxBars       = input.int(0, "Protected level expires after (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 500, group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "0 = never expire, which is now the default. Expiry matters much less since a level is also retired the moment price CLOSES through it, and at 60 bars it was throwing away a third of all levels untouched.")
float msMaxDepthAtr   = input.float(0.0, "Max sweep depth (ATR)",  minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "How far price may WICK beyond the level and still count. 0 = no cap, which is now the default: a candle that closes back on the right side has reclaimed the level however deep the wick went, and a genuine breakdown is already caught by the close-through rule.")
float msMinReclaimAtr = input.float(0.0, "Min reclaim beyond level (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "Extra distance the close must clear the level by. 0 = any close on the right side, which is now the default. Raise it if you get sweeps that close back over the level by a hair.")

// ── Trend filter — the whole point of this fork ──────────
// LuxAlgo's version has ONE degree of structure and therefore cannot ask this question.
// Ours has two, so the filter is our own external engine rather than a bolted-on average.
string msTrendMode = input.string("Trending market", "Trend filter", options = ["Off", "Trending market", "Trending + same direction"], group = GRP_TREND, tooltip = "Off = every sweep prints.\n\nTrending market (default) = the EXTERNAL structure must have continued at least once since its last change of character. Directionless on purpose: it asks whether the market is trending, not which way. In chop the external structure keeps flipping, the run never builds, and sweeps are refused.\n\nTrending + same direction ALSO demands the sweep point the same way as the last external break. 🔴 That was the old default and it refused ~100% of sweeps — our internal structure is rebuilt inside the PULLBACK of each external leg, so its first setup points against the external break by construction. Kept as an option, not a default, and only useful once you have measured it.")
int    msMinBos    = input.int(0, "Min INTERNAL continuation breaks", minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = GRP_TREND, tooltip = "⚠ 1 DOES NOTHING. A protected level only exists because a continuation break created it, so the count is already at least 1 by the time any sweep can happen — the gate was inert at its old default of 1 and looked like it was working. 2 or more is the first value that filters anything. 0 = off.")
bool   msBlockOnExt = input.bool(true, "Disarm on opposing external SOS", group = GRP_TREND, tooltip = "An external change of character against the armed direction throws the level away. This is the case the LuxAlgo original gets wrong: there, only the opposite BOS disarms, so a stale level stays live through a whole counter-leg.")

// ── Style / diagnostics ──────────────────────────────────
color msBullCol  = input.color(#089981, "Bullish sweep",  group = GRP_MSSTY)
color msBearCol  = input.color(#f23645, "Bearish sweep",  group = GRP_MSSTY)
color msLevelCol = input.color(#ff9800, "Protected level", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Amber by default rather than pale blue, so the armed level does not read as another structure line. It turns the sweep colour on the bar it is taken.")
bool  msShowStats = input.bool(true, "Show stats table", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Counts raw sweeps against signalled ones. Read them together — 'signalled' alone says nothing about whether the filter earned its place.")

// ⚠ These are declared LAST on purpose. TradingView keys a chart's saved input values off
// declaration order WITHIN EACH TYPE, so anything new has to sit after every existing input of
// its own type or it silently resets the ones below it on a chart that is already tuned.
bool   msShowZone   = input.bool(true, "Shade the swept wick", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Fill the gap between the protected level and the wick that took it. This is the part worth seeing — it is the liquidity grab itself.")
bool   msShowBg     = input.bool(true, "Tint the signal bar", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Colour the whole bar's background on a signal, so a sweep is findable when scrolled out.")
int    msLevelWidth = input.int(2, "Protected level thickness", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = GRP_MSSTY)
string msMarkSizeIn = input.string("Large", "Sweep marker size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "The marker is a solid triangle rather than a text label, so it cannot be mistaken for one of the structure tags.")
bool   msRejectText  = input.bool(false, "Label rejected sweeps with the reason", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Print the failing gate next to the grey cross. Useful while you are deciding whether the trend filter earns its place; noisy afterwards.")
color  msRejectCol   = input.color(#787b86, "Rejected sweep", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Rejected sweeps are deliberately a neutral grey — never a dimmed green or red, because a washed-out green reads as a weak BUY rather than as no trade at all.")
string msRejectSizeIn = input.string("Small", "Rejected marker size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = GRP_MSSTY)
bool   msShowLevelTag = input.bool(true, "Tag the armed level", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Put a tag on the right end of every armed level reading direction, level type and price — e.g. \"▲ iHL 3891.20\". Without it a dashed line is just a line: you cannot tell a protected LOW waiting to be swept downward from a protected HIGH waiting to be swept upward.")
color  msArmBullCol   = input.color(#26a69a, "Armed level — bullish (protected iHL)", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "A protected higher low. Price is expected to dip THROUGH it and close back above — a long.")
color  msArmBearCol   = input.color(#ef5350, "Armed level — bearish (protected iLH)", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "A protected lower high. Price is expected to poke ABOVE it and close back below — a short.")
color  msSweptBullCol = input.color(#7e57c2, "Taken level — was a protected iHL", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Deliberately NOT a shade of the armed colour. WAITING and TAKEN are different states of the level, and a darker green reads as \"the same thing, dimmer\" rather than as \"this one is finished\".")
color  msSweptBearCol = input.color(#ff9800, "Taken level — was a protected iLH", group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "Same reasoning as the bullish one. Purple and amber sit far from the teal/red armed pair and far from each other, so all four states are separable at a glance.")
string msLevelColMode = input.string("By direction", "Armed level colour", options = ["By direction", "Single colour"], group = GRP_MSSTY, tooltip = "By direction = green for a protected low, red for a protected high, so the line itself says which way the trade would be. Single colour falls back to the \"Protected level\" colour above.")

// ⚠ Appended after every existing input of their own type, same reason as the block above.
int   msMinExtBos = input.int(1, "Min EXTERNAL continuation breaks", minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = GRP_TREND, tooltip = "This is the trending-versus-chopping measure. Counts how many times the EXTERNAL structure has continued in its own direction since its last change of character. In a trend that number builds; in chop the structure keeps reversing and it sits at 0. Directionless on purpose. Only read when the Trend filter is not Off.")
bool  msOneShot   = input.bool(false, "Kill the level after one failed touch", group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "🔴 This was HARDCODED ON and is the reason most levels never produced anything. The first candle to poke through decided, and a level that failed by a hair was deleted even though the next candle might have swept it perfectly. Off by default now: a level survives failed touches and keeps waiting. It is still retired the moment price CLOSES through it, which is a real break rather than a failed sweep.")
bool  msReqGreen  = input.bool(false, "Sweep candle must close in its own direction", group = GRP_MSS, tooltip = "Was hardcoded ON. Demands a green candle on a bullish sweep, red on a bearish one. A genuine wick-and-reclaim often closes the other colour while still finishing back on the right side of the level, so this refused real sweeps. Off by default.")

string msRejectSize = msRejectSizeIn == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : msRejectSizeIn == "Normal" ? size.normal : msRejectSizeIn == "Large" ? size.large : size.small

// Structure draws in text labels; sweeps draw in solid triangles, offset off the wick by a
// fraction of ATR. Different SHAPE, different DISTANCE — that is what stops the two layers
// reading as one pile of tags on a busy chart.
string msMarkSize = msMarkSizeIn == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : msMarkSizeIn == "Small" ? size.small : msMarkSizeIn == "Normal" ? size.normal : msMarkSizeIn == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.large

float msAtr = ta.atr(14)

// ── Trend run tracking ───────────────────────────────────
// An iSOS is a change of character, so it STARTS a run at zero. Each iBOS after it is one
// continuation. This is the same shape as mpc_d_strategy.pine's dTrendBos and is deliberately
// counted here rather than read off the engine, which does not expose a run length.
var int msRunDir   = 0
var int msRunCount = 0

if int_bull_sos
    msRunDir   := 1
    msRunCount := 0
if int_bear_sos
    msRunDir   := -1
    msRunCount := 0
if int_bull_bos
    msRunCount := msRunDir == 1 ? msRunCount + 1 : 1
    msRunDir   := 1
if int_bear_bos
    msRunCount := msRunDir == -1 ? msRunCount + 1 : 1
    msRunDir   := -1

// ── External run tracking — the trending-vs-chopping measure ─
// 🔴 THIS REPLACES THE OLD DIRECTION TEST, WHICH WAS THE BUG. `st.dir` is the direction of the
// last EXTERNAL break. Our internal structure is wiped and reseeded on every external break,
// and it reseeds tracking the PULLBACK — so the first protected level of every external leg
// points AGAINST st.dir by construction. A filter demanding they agree therefore refused
// essentially every sweep, and the chart read as "too strict" when it was asking an impossible
// question. Counting external CONTINUATIONS instead asks the question that was actually wanted:
// is this market trending, or is it turning over every leg. It has no direction in it at all.
// ⚠ An external SOS also sets bull_bos/bear_bos in the engine, so SOS must be tested FIRST.
var int msExtRun = 0
if st.bull_sos or st.bear_sos
    msExtRun := 0
else if st.bull_bos or st.bear_bos
    msExtRun += 1

// ── Armed state ──────────────────────────────────────────
var int   msArmDir   = 0
var float msArmLevel = na
var int   msArmLoc   = na
var int   msArmBar   = na
var line  msArmLine  = na

// ── Counters, for the stats table ────────────────────────
var int msCntArmed    = 0
var int msCntRaw      = 0
var int msCntSignal   = 0
var int msCntFiltered = 0
var int msCntFailed   = 0
var int msCntBroken   = 0
var int msCntExpired  = 0
// The three ways a level can leave WITHOUT price ever resolving it. They were pooled into an
// unlabelled remainder, and "died young" and "superseded by a fresher level" mean opposite
// things — the first says the levels are not surviving, the second is ordinary housekeeping.
var int msCntShiftInt = 0
var int msCntShiftExt = 0
var int msCntReplaced = 0

// ── Sweep test ───────────────────────────────────────────
// ⚠ THIS BLOCK RUNS BEFORE THE ARM BLOCK ON PURPOSE. On an iBOS bar the level being armed is
// brand new, and price on that same bar has usually already traded through where it sits. If
// the order were reversed, a fresh level would sweep itself on the bar it was created.
bool msWickLow  = msArmDir ==  1 and not na(msArmLevel) and low  < msArmLevel
bool msWickHigh = msArmDir == -1 and not na(msArmLevel) and high > msArmLevel

float msDepthLow  = msWickLow  ? msArmLevel - low  : na
float msDepthHigh = msWickHigh ? high - msArmLevel : na
bool  msDepthOkLo = msMaxDepthAtr <= 0 or na(msAtr) or msDepthLow  <= msMaxDepthAtr * msAtr
bool  msDepthOkHi = msMaxDepthAtr <= 0 or na(msAtr) or msDepthHigh <= msMaxDepthAtr * msAtr

float msReclaimBuf = na(msAtr) ? 0.0 : msMinReclaimAtr * msAtr
bool  msReclaimLo  = close > msArmLevel + msReclaimBuf and (not msReqGreen or close > open)
bool  msReclaimHi  = close < msArmLevel - msReclaimBuf and (not msReqGreen or close < open)

bool msSweepLow  = barstate.isconfirmed and msWickLow  and msDepthOkLo and msReclaimLo
bool msSweepHigh = barstate.isconfirmed and msWickHigh and msDepthOkHi and msReclaimHi

// 🔴 A FAILED TOUCH IS NOT A BREAK, AND CONFLATING THEM WAS THE SECOND BUG. The old code
// retired a level on ANY poke through that did not qualify — so a level that missed by a hair
// was deleted before the candle that would have swept it properly ever arrived. Two different
// events now:
//   TOUCH FAIL — the wick went through and the candle did not qualify. The level SURVIVES
//                and keeps waiting, unless msOneShot puts the old behaviour back.
//   BREAK      — price CLOSED through and stayed there. That is not a failed sweep, it is the
//                level being taken out, and it always retires it. No wick required: a gap that
//                opens and closes beyond the level counts too.
bool msTouchFailLow  = barstate.isconfirmed and msWickLow  and not msSweepLow
bool msTouchFailHigh = barstate.isconfirmed and msWickHigh and not msSweepHigh
bool msBreakLow  = barstate.isconfirmed and msArmDir ==  1 and not na(msArmLevel) and close < msArmLevel
bool msBreakHigh = barstate.isconfirmed and msArmDir == -1 and not na(msArmLevel) and close > msArmLevel
bool msFailLow   = msBreakLow  or (msOneShot and msTouchFailLow)
bool msFailHigh  = msBreakHigh or (msOneShot and msTouchFailHigh)

// Counted DISJOINT. A bar that closes through has also wicked through, so it satisfies both
// tests — counting it in both rows would inflate "failed touches" with levels that were simply
// taken out, and those two numbers call for opposite responses. A break wins.
if msBreakLow or msBreakHigh
    msCntBroken += 1
else if msTouchFailLow or msTouchFailHigh
    msCntFailed += 1

// ── The trend gate ───────────────────────────────────────
// Evaluated at SWEEP time, never at arm time. The trend has to still be intact when the
// signal prints, and arming unconditionally is what lets the stats table report what the
// filter actually removed.
bool msTrendOk    = msTrendMode == "Off" or msExtRun >= msMinExtBos
bool msDirOkLong  = msTrendMode != "Trending + same direction" or st.dir ==  1
bool msDirOkShort = msTrendMode != "Trending + same direction" or st.dir == -1
bool msRunOk      = msRunCount >= msMinBos

bool msSignalLow  = msSweepLow  and msTrendOk and msDirOkLong  and msRunOk
bool msSignalHigh = msSweepHigh and msTrendOk and msDirOkShort and msRunOk

// ── Why a sweep was refused ──────────────────────────────
// 🔴 The first version of this tooltip printed the external direction and the break count and
// left the reader to work out which one failed. On a bearish sweep refused by a bullish trend
// it therefore read "External direction: bullish / breaks: 1 (need 1)" — two lines that both
// look like passes, on a marker that means NO. A verdict has to name the gate that failed and
// the direction the sweep WAS, or it is not a verdict, it is a data dump.
string msExtTxt = st.dir == 1 ? "bullish" : st.dir == -1 ? "bearish" : "none yet"

f_msWhy(bool trendOk, bool dirOk, bool runOk, string want) =>
    string _head = not trendOk ? "MARKET NOT TRENDING" : not dirOk ? "TREND DIRECTION" : not runOk ? "INTERNAL MATURITY" : "—"
    "REJECTED — failed on " + _head + "\n\n" + (trendOk ? "PASS" : "FAIL") + "  trending: " + str.tostring(msExtRun) + " external continuation(s), needs " + str.tostring(msMinExtBos) + "\n" + (dirOk ? "PASS" : "FAIL") + "  direction: external is " + msExtTxt + ", needs " + want + (msTrendMode == "Trending + same direction" ? "" : "  (not checked)") + "\n" + (runOk ? "PASS" : "FAIL") + "  internal maturity: " + str.tostring(msRunCount) + " break(s), needs " + str.tostring(msMinBos)

f_msWhyShort(bool trendOk, bool dirOk, bool runOk) =>
    not trendOk ? "not trending" : not dirOk ? "wrong trend" : not runOk ? "trend too young" : ""

// ── Draw and disarm ──────────────────────────────────────
// The armed level carries a live tag on its right end. It is a separate object from the line
// because it has to be re-anchored every bar as the line extends, and because on a sweep it is
// REPLACED (with a "SWEPT" tag frozen at the sweep bar) rather than deleted.
var label msArmLbl = na

f_msDropTag() =>
    if not na(msArmLbl)
        label.delete(msArmLbl)
    int _dropped = 0

f_msCloseLine() =>
    if not na(msArmLine)
        line.set_x2(msArmLine, bar_index)
        line.set_extend(msArmLine, extend.none)
    int _done = 0

if msSweepLow
    msCntRaw += 1
    if msSignalLow
        msCntSignal += 1
        if msShow
            float _off = na(msAtr) ? 0.0 : msAtr * 0.5
            label.new(bar_index, low - _off, "", style = label.style_triangleup, color = msBullCol, size = msMarkSize, tooltip = "SIGNAL — bullish HL sweep, all gates passed\n\nProtected iHL: " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick) + "\nHeld for " + str.tostring(bar_index - msArmBar) + " bars\nContinuation breaks in run: " + str.tostring(msRunCount))
            // The level lights up in the sweep colour, so the chart shows WHICH level was taken
            // rather than just that something happened here.
            // Two layers, two colour families, on purpose. The LEVEL that was taken draws in
            // the taken colour — solid, one step thicker, plus its wick box and its tag. The
            // TRADE draws in the direction colour — the triangle and the bar tint. Mixing them
            // is what made "waiting" and "taken" look like the same thing.
            line.new(msArmLoc, msArmLevel, bar_index, msArmLevel, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = msSweptBullCol, style = line.style_solid, width = msLevelWidth + 1)
            if msShowZone
                box.new(bar_index - 1, msArmLevel, bar_index + 1, low, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(msSweptBullCol, 30), bgcolor = color.new(msSweptBullCol, 75))
            // Names the level that was taken, at the price it was taken at. "A sweep happened
            // here" and "THIS level was swept" are different facts and only the second one is
            // actionable — it is the stop.
            if msShowLevelTag
                label.new(bar_index + 2, msArmLevel, "▲ TAKEN iHL " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color(na), textcolor = msSweptBullCol, size = size.small)
    else
        msCntFiltered += 1
        if msShowFiltered
            // Same LANE as a real signal — one ATR off the wick — so valid and refused sweeps
            // line up and can be compared by eye. Everything else about them differs: a cross
            // instead of a filled triangle, neutral grey instead of the direction colour, and
            // no wick box and no bar tint. Shape, colour and supporting marks all disagree with
            // a signal, which is what makes the two unmistakable at a glance.
            float _roff = na(msAtr) ? 0.0 : msAtr * 0.5
            label.new(bar_index, low - _roff, msRejectText ? f_msWhyShort(msTrendOk, msDirOkLong, msRunOk) : "", style = label.style_xcross, color = msRejectCol, textcolor = msRejectCol, size = msRejectSize, tooltip = "Bullish HL sweep — NOT TAKEN\n\n" + f_msWhy(msTrendOk, msDirOkLong, msRunOk, "bullish"))
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir := 0
    msArmLevel := na
    msArmLoc := na
    msArmBar := na
    msArmLine := na
    msArmLbl := na
else if msFailLow
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir := 0
    msArmLevel := na
    msArmLoc := na
    msArmBar := na
    msArmLine := na
    msArmLbl := na

if msSweepHigh
    msCntRaw += 1
    if msSignalHigh
        msCntSignal += 1
        if msShow
            float _off = na(msAtr) ? 0.0 : msAtr * 0.5
            label.new(bar_index, high + _off, "", style = label.style_triangledown, color = msBearCol, size = msMarkSize, tooltip = "SIGNAL — bearish LH sweep, all gates passed\n\nProtected iLH: " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick) + "\nHeld for " + str.tostring(bar_index - msArmBar) + " bars\nContinuation breaks in run: " + str.tostring(msRunCount))
            line.new(msArmLoc, msArmLevel, bar_index, msArmLevel, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = msSweptBearCol, style = line.style_solid, width = msLevelWidth + 1)
            if msShowZone
                box.new(bar_index - 1, high, bar_index + 1, msArmLevel, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(msSweptBearCol, 30), bgcolor = color.new(msSweptBearCol, 75))
            if msShowLevelTag
                label.new(bar_index + 2, msArmLevel, "▼ TAKEN iLH " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color(na), textcolor = msSweptBearCol, size = size.small)
    else
        msCntFiltered += 1
        if msShowFiltered
            float _roff = na(msAtr) ? 0.0 : msAtr * 0.5
            label.new(bar_index, high + _roff, msRejectText ? f_msWhyShort(msTrendOk, msDirOkShort, msRunOk) : "", style = label.style_xcross, color = msRejectCol, textcolor = msRejectCol, size = msRejectSize, tooltip = "Bearish LH sweep — NOT TAKEN\n\n" + f_msWhy(msTrendOk, msDirOkShort, msRunOk, "bearish"))
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir := 0
    msArmLevel := na
    msArmLoc := na
    msArmBar := na
    msArmLine := na
    msArmLbl := na
else if msFailHigh
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir := 0
    msArmLevel := na
    msArmLoc := na
    msArmBar := na
    msArmLine := na
    msArmLbl := na

// ── Invalidation that is NOT a sweep ─────────────────────
// 🔴 This is the defect in the LuxAlgo original, fixed. There, the armed direction survives an
// opposite CHOCH and is only overwritten by an opposite BOS — which needs a character change
// PLUS a second break — so a stale bullish level stays live through an entire confirmed
// bearish leg and can print a long signal into it. Here any shift against the armed direction,
// at either degree, throws the level away.
bool msShiftAgainst = (msArmDir ==  1 and (int_bear_sos or int_bear_bos)) or (msArmDir == -1 and (int_bull_sos or int_bull_bos))
bool msExtAgainst   = msBlockOnExt and ((msArmDir == 1 and st.bear_sos) or (msArmDir == -1 and st.bull_sos))
bool msStale        = msMaxBars > 0 and msArmDir != 0 and not na(msArmBar) and (bar_index - msArmBar) > msMaxBars

if msArmDir != 0 and (msShiftAgainst or msExtAgainst or msStale)
    // Disjoint, in precedence order, so the rows sum. Internal shift first because it is the
    // nearer cause: if internal structure has already turned, the external SOS behind it is
    // reporting the same event one degree up.
    if msShiftAgainst
        msCntShiftInt += 1
    else if msExtAgainst
        msCntShiftExt += 1
    else
        msCntExpired += 1
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir := 0
    msArmLevel := na
    msArmLoc := na
    msArmBar := na
    msArmLine := na
    msArmLbl := na

// ── Arm on a continuation break ──────────────────────────
// Armed UNCONDITIONALLY — the trend filter is applied to the signal, not to the arming, so
// that the stats table can report what it removed. i_last_hl / i_last_lh are the engine's own
// confirmed pullback extremes; they are read rather than re-derived, so this file cannot
// disagree with the structure drawn on the chart.
// ⚠ The freshness test is not defensive noise. The engine writes i_last_hl only when it has a
// tracked pullback extreme to write; when it does not, the variable KEEPS ITS PREVIOUS VALUE
// rather than going na, so `not na(i_last_hl)` alone would happily arm on an iHL left over from
// an earlier internal cycle. Requiring the LOCATION to have moved this bar is what makes the
// level the one this break actually left behind. Stale-level arming is the exact defect this
// fork exists to fix; it must not be reintroduced from the other end.
bool msArmBull = int_bull_bos and not na(i_last_hl) and (na(i_last_hl_loc[1]) or i_last_hl_loc != i_last_hl_loc[1])
bool msArmBear = int_bear_bos and not na(i_last_lh) and (na(i_last_lh_loc[1]) or i_last_lh_loc != i_last_lh_loc[1])

if msArmBull
    // Counted BEFORE msArmDir is overwritten. Arming while a level is still live means a
    // fresher break moved the level up (or down) — the old one was never tested by price.
    if msArmDir != 0
        msCntReplaced += 1
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir   := 1
    msArmLevel := i_last_hl
    msArmLoc   := i_last_hl_loc
    msArmBar   := bar_index
    msCntArmed += 1
    color _c = msLevelColMode == "Single colour" ? msLevelCol : msArmBullCol
    msArmLine  := msShowLevel ? line.new(msArmLoc, msArmLevel, bar_index, msArmLevel, xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right, color = _c, style = line.style_dashed, width = msLevelWidth) : na
    msArmLbl   := msShowLevelTag ? label.new(bar_index + 2, msArmLevel, "▲ iHL " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color(na), textcolor = _c, size = size.small, tooltip = "Protected higher low, armed by a bullish iBOS.\nWaiting for price to dip through it and CLOSE back above.\nThat close would be a long.") : na

if msArmBear
    // Counted BEFORE msArmDir is overwritten. Arming while a level is still live means a
    // fresher break moved the level up (or down) — the old one was never tested by price.
    if msArmDir != 0
        msCntReplaced += 1
    f_msCloseLine()
    f_msDropTag()
    msArmDir   := -1
    msArmLevel := i_last_lh
    msArmLoc   := i_last_lh_loc
    msArmBar   := bar_index
    msCntArmed += 1
    color _c = msLevelColMode == "Single colour" ? msLevelCol : msArmBearCol
    msArmLine  := msShowLevel ? line.new(msArmLoc, msArmLevel, bar_index, msArmLevel, xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right, color = _c, style = line.style_dashed, width = msLevelWidth) : na
    msArmLbl   := msShowLevelTag ? label.new(bar_index + 2, msArmLevel, "▼ iLH " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color(na), textcolor = _c, size = size.small, tooltip = "Protected lower high, armed by a bearish iBOS.\nWaiting for price to poke above it and CLOSE back below.\nThat close would be a short.") : na

// ── Keep the live tag on the right end of the line ───────
// The line uses extend.right, so its visible end moves every bar while the label does not.
// Without this the tag strands itself back at the bar the level was armed on.
if not na(msArmLbl)
    label.set_x(msArmLbl, bar_index + 2)

// ── Stats table ──────────────────────────────────────────
// Read "raw" against "signalled". A filter that removes most of the sample and leaves the same
// hit rate has not helped; it has just made the sample smaller. That question is settled by
// replaying it, not by this table — the table only tells you how big the difference IS.
//
// ⚠ EVERY ARMED LEVEL NOW HAS TO LAND IN EXACTLY ONE OUTCOME ROW, and the last row proves it.
// The rows below used to account for 75 of 154 levels and the other 79 sat in an unlabelled
// remainder that nobody could see, which is how a diagnostic starts lying by omission. The
// "Unaccounted" row is a self-check: it is 0 when the model is complete, and any other number
// means a level left by a path this table does not model. Read it before reading anything else.
// ⚠ A failed touch only ENDS a level when msOneShot is on, so it only joins the sum then.
int msAccounted   = msCntRaw + msCntBroken + (msOneShot ? msCntFailed : 0) + msCntExpired + msCntShiftInt + msCntShiftExt + msCntReplaced + (msArmDir != 0 ? 1 : 0)
int msUnaccounted = msCntArmed - msAccounted

var table msTbl = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 17, border_width = 1)

if barstate.islast and msShowStats
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 0, "MSS Sweeps (MPC)", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = color.new(msLevelCol, 70))
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 0, msTrendMode == "Off" ? "filter OFF" : "trending run " + str.tostring(msExtRun) + "/" + str.tostring(msMinExtBos), text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = color.new(msLevelCol, 70))
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 1, "Levels armed",   text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 1, str.tostring(msCntArmed),  text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 2, "Sweeps (raw)",   text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 2, str.tostring(msCntRaw),    text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 3, "Signalled",      text_color = msBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 3, str.tostring(msCntSignal), text_color = msBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 4, "Cut by filter",  text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 4, str.tostring(msCntFiltered) + (msCntRaw > 0 ? "  (" + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * msCntFiltered / msCntRaw)) + "%)" : ""), text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    // Touches and breaks are counted apart on purpose. A high touch count with the level
    // surviving is the trigger being picky; a high BREAK count means the levels are simply
    // being taken out, which is a different problem and needs a different answer.
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 5, "Failed touches", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 5, str.tostring(msCntFailed) + (msOneShot ? "  (each ends a level)" : "  (level survives)"), text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 6, "Closed through", text_color = msBearCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 6, str.tostring(msCntBroken), text_color = msBearCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 7, "Structure turned", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 7, str.tostring(msCntShiftInt) + " internal / " + str.tostring(msCntShiftExt) + " external", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 8, "Replaced by newer", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 8, str.tostring(msCntReplaced), text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 9, "Expired unused", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 9, msMaxBars > 0 ? str.tostring(msCntExpired) : "— (no expiry)", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 10, "Armed now",      text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 10, msArmDir == 1 ? "bullish @ " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick) : msArmDir == -1 ? "bearish @ " + str.tostring(msArmLevel, format.mintick) : "—", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 11, "Unaccounted", text_color = msUnaccounted == 0 ? color.gray : msBearCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 11, str.tostring(msUnaccounted) + (msUnaccounted == 0 ? "  (rows sum)" : "  ⚠ rows do NOT sum"), text_color = msUnaccounted == 0 ? color.gray : msBearCol, text_size = size.small)
    // The legend is not decoration. The one question a reader has in front of this chart is
    // "is that mark a trade or not", and answering it in a tooltip means it is only answered
    // for whoever hovers.
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 12, "▲▼ solid", text_color = msBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 12, "SIGNAL — shaded wick, tinted bar", text_color = msBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 13, "✕ grey",  text_color = msRejectCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 13, "swept, refused — hover for the gate", text_color = msRejectCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 14, "▲ iHL",  text_color = msArmBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 14, "armed low — dip through, close above = long", text_color = msArmBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 15, "▼ iLH",  text_color = msArmBearCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 15, "armed high — poke above, close below = short", text_color = msArmBearCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 0, 16, "━ solid", text_color = msSweptBullCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(msTbl, 1, 16, "TAKEN — purple was a low, amber was a high", text_color = msSweptBearCol, text_size = size.small)

// ── Signal bar tint ──────────────────────────────────────
// bgcolor() has to be a top-level call, so it cannot live inside the drawing blocks above.
// It is the layer that survives being zoomed out, where a marker is a few pixels.
bgcolor(msShowBg and msSignalLow ? color.new(msBullCol, 85) : msShowBg and msSignalHigh ? color.new(msBearCol, 85) : na, title = "MSS signal bar")

// NOTE — there is deliberately no "signals are switched off" warning here any more. It existed
// because the engine's internal state machine was gated on the "Show Internal Structure"
// display toggle. That gate is now forced open (see the engine block), so all three Market
// Structure display boxes can be unticked for a clean chart and every signal keeps firing.

//============================================================
//  TRADING SESSIONS — ported from mpc_strategy.pine
//============================================================
// ⚠ ONE TOGGLE, DEFAULT OFF, EVERYTHING ELSE HARDCODED. That is the standing contract for a
// section-10 drawing group (indicators/strategies/CLAUDE.md): Aaron does not configure session
// windows, timezones or colours, so exposing them would be six inputs nobody moves and six more
// declaration slots that reset saved values whenever they are touched.
//
// ⚠ THE VALUES ARE COPIED, NOT CHOSEN. Windows, timezones and colours are the ones every other
// Pine file here runs, including the DST-aware city clocks — each session keeps its OWN city's
// time zone rather than a fixed GMT offset, which is what makes Tokyo/London/New York stay
// correct across the four changeovers a year. A fixed offset was the old form and it drifted.
//
// ⚠ Ported from the mpc_assistant.pine copy rather than the strategy copy, and the difference is
// DEAD CODE ONLY: the strategies still carry the session open/close and average lines behind
// three flags hardcoded false, so those branches cannot execute. The drawing is identical — the
// box, its dotted border and its name label — and this file has a compile-token budget to
// respect. If those lines are ever wanted, they are in mpc_strategy.pine.
//
// ⚠ The input is declared HERE, at the very end of the file, so it sits after every existing
// bool. TradingView keys saved values off declaration order within each type.
bool showSessionsInput = input.bool(false, "Show Sessions", group = "10 · Drawing: sessions", display = display.none, tooltip = "Tokyo / London / New York session boxes, in the same windows, timezones and colours every other MPC Pine draws them. Draw-only: no signal, level or filter in this file reads a session.")

bool showSessions         = showSessionsInput
bool showSessionNames     = false
// ⚠ FALSE is the strategy default and is deliberately kept. It limits the boxes to the CURRENT
// week, anchored at Sunday 00:00 New York — so scrolling back through history shows no session
// shading. Flip this constant to true for the mpc_assistant behaviour (every session, all
// history) if reviewing old signals against sessions is what you are here for.
bool showHistoricSessions = false

bool   showFirst         = true
string firstSessionName  = "Tokyo"
string firstSessionTime  = "0900-1800"
string firstSessionTZ    = "Asia/Tokyo"
color  firstSessionColor = color.new(#FF5252, 92)

bool   showSecond         = true
string secondSessionName  = "London"
string secondSessionTime  = "0800-1700"
string secondSessionTZ    = "Europe/London"
color  secondSessionColor = color.new(#2962FF, 92)

bool   showThird         = true
string thirdSessionName  = "New York"
string thirdSessionTime  = "0800-1700"
string thirdSessionTZ    = "America/New_York"
color  thirdSessionColor = color.new(#FFEB3B, 90)

type SessionDisplay
    box   sessionBox
    label sessionLabel

type SessionInfo
    color  color
    string name
    string session
    string timezone
    SessionDisplay active = na

method setName(SessionDisplay this, string name) =>
    this.sessionLabel.set_y(this.sessionBox.get_bottom())
    this.sessionLabel.set_text(showSessionNames ? name : "")

method createSessionDisplay(SessionInfo this) =>
    boxColor    = this.color
    opaqueColor = color.new(boxColor, 0)
    dis = SessionDisplay.new(
      sessionBox   = box.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, low, bgcolor = boxColor, border_color = color.new(boxColor, 40), border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_dotted),
      sessionLabel = label.new(bar_index + 2, low, "", style = label.style_label_upper_left, textalign = text.align_left, textcolor = opaqueColor, color = color(na)))
    dis.setName(this.name)
    this.active := dis

method updateSessionDisplay(SessionInfo this) =>
    sessionDisp = this.active
    sessionBox  = sessionDisp.sessionBox
    sessionBox.set_top(math.max(sessionBox.get_top(), high))
    sessionBox.set_bottom(math.min(sessionBox.get_bottom(), low))
    sessionBox.set_right(bar_index)
    sessionDisp.setName(this.name)
    sessionDisp

method update(SessionInfo this) =>
    bool isChange = timeframe.change("1D")
    if not na(time("", this.session, this.timezone))
        if na(this.active) or isChange
            this.createSessionDisplay()
        else
            this.updateSessionDisplay()
    else if not na(this.active)
        this.active := na

getSessionInfos() =>
    array<SessionInfo> sessionInfos = array.new<SessionInfo>()
    if showFirst and showSessions
        sessionInfos.push(SessionInfo.new(firstSessionColor, firstSessionName, firstSessionTime, firstSessionTZ))
    if showSecond and showSessions
        sessionInfos.push(SessionInfo.new(secondSessionColor, secondSessionName, secondSessionTime, secondSessionTZ))
    if showThird and showSessions
        sessionInfos.push(SessionInfo.new(thirdSessionColor, thirdSessionName, thirdSessionTime, thirdSessionTZ))
    sessionInfos

// Anchored to the CALENDAR week rather than a rolling seven days, so mid-week it cannot bleed
// into last week's boxes.
int  msNyMidnight      = timestamp("America/New_York", year(timenow, "America/New_York"), month(timenow, "America/New_York"), dayofmonth(timenow, "America/New_York"), 0, 0)
int  msDaysSinceSunday = dayofweek(timenow, "America/New_York") - dayofweek.sunday
int  msWeekStart       = msNyMidnight - msDaysSinceSunday * 86400000
bool withinSessionDays = showHistoricSessions or time >= msWeekStart

var array<SessionInfo> sessionInfos = getSessionInfos()
if showSessions and timeframe.isintraday and withinSessionDays
    for info in sessionInfos
        info.update()

// ── Alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every one of these is confirmed-bar only. The engine's breaks already require
// barstate.isconfirmed and the sweep test requires it again, so nothing here can fire on a
// signal that later un-prints.
alertcondition(msSignalLow,  "MSS Bullish HL Sweep", "Protected higher low swept and reclaimed, with the trend filter passing.")
alertcondition(msSignalHigh, "MSS Bearish LH Sweep", "Protected lower high swept and reclaimed, with the trend filter passing.")
alertcondition(int_bull_bos, "Internal Bullish BOS", "Bullish iBOS — a protected higher low is now armed.")
alertcondition(int_bear_bos, "Internal Bearish BOS", "Bearish iBOS — a protected lower high is now armed.")

if msSignalLow
    alert("MSS Sweeps (MPC): bullish HL sweep on " + syminfo.ticker + " (" + timeframe.period + ") @ " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

if msSignalHigh
    alert("MSS Sweeps (MPC): bearish LH sweep on " + syminfo.ticker + " (" + timeframe.period + ") @ " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
